  "modelName": "Making Agreements — first what the rules need, then the rules",
  "modelNote": "Ostrom's Institutional Grammar (IG 2.0, Frantz and Siddiki 2021; Crawford and Ostrom 1995) drawn as plain questions a group answers, shown on one community-garden bylaw. Two kinds of agreement: creating agreements (IG constitutive statements) come first, because they make the roles and things the rules need; rules about what people do (IG regulative statements) come second. WHEN? and OR ELSE? belong to both kinds. The canvas uses plain words only; every question node carries its IG term, symbol, definition, synonyms, and example in props and in its hover note. IG Core only. Layout by Marc Pierson. Marc Pierson and Claude Opus 5.5, September 2026.",
